 "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened the SEV2 incident, which paged on-call.\n\n- **What was wrong:** v2.3.1 was live in all three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), failing health checks with an 18% error rate.\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 was the most recent release that was healthy in production. I rolled back to it in all three regions. A follow-up status check shows the service healthy everywhere, with the error rate down to 0.2%. No approval was needed because v2.3.0 had already been healthy in production.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 (SEV2, checkout-api) explains the failure, the rollback and the recovery. As a follow-up, it asks for the root cause and why v2.3.1 was promoted even though its test build (v2.3.1-rc) had already failed health checks in staging.", "type": "text"}]}]}